65,3,1,talk,Rin,,Option C is the only one that doesn't waste our time! No morning setup and no packing boxes. I'm voting for Fixed Desks by Function!,"{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,1,talk,Toshio,,Option C is the most fiscally sound choice. It avoids the recurring costs of re-running power and network that Options A and B would inevitably trigger. I vote for Fixed Desks by Function.,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,1,talk,Mizuki,,"Option C is the only way to ensure we handle the daylight issue and seat quality transparently. It prevents a ""race"" for the best spots. I vote for Fixed Desks by Function.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,1,talk,Shion,,Option C is the only logical choice. It protects our ergonomic settings and shields us from the noise of the printer. I vote for Fixed Desks by Function.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,1,talk,Yumi,,I'm voting for Option C too! It's the best way to make sure we stay connected and keep our great conversations going without any stress. Fixed Desks by Function it is!,"{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
